@i{Name} is a value-flavoured word, @i{...} is optional additional
addressing information, e.g., for a value-flavoured field.  At
run-time, perform the @i{+to @i{name}} semantics: if @i{name} (with
the same additional addressing information) pushed @i{value1}
before, change it to push @i{value2}, the sum of the @i{value1} and
@i{value}.  The type of @i{value} depends on the type of @i{name}
(see the defining word for @i{name} for the actual type).  An
alternative syntax is to write @code{+>@i{name}}.

