#line 63 "kernel/input.fs"
make-doc read-line c_addr u1 wfileid -- u2 flag wior  ) file
Reads a line from @i{wfileid} into the buffer at @i{c_addr u1}.
Gforth supports all three common line terminators: LF, CR and
CRLF.  A non-zero @i{wior} indicates an error.  A false
@i{flag} indicates that @code{read-line} has been invoked at
the end of the file. @i{u2} indicates the line length (without
terminator): @i{u2}<@i{u1} indicates that the line is @i{u2}
chars long; @i{u2}=@i{u1} indicates that the line is at least
@i{u1} chars long, @i{u1} chars of the buffer have been
filled with chars from the line, and the next slice of the line
will be read with the next @code{read-line}.  If the line is
@i{u1} chars long, the first @code{read-line} returns
@i{u2}=@i{u1} and the next read-line returns @i{u2}=0.

